      <div type="clause" n="42">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 42</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="340" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.1-3"/> hwa gehadodne man bende<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.27"/> oððon beate oððon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.28"/> swyðe gebysmrige, bete wið hine, swa swa hit riht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.1-3"/> sy, ⁊ bisceope<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.2-3"/> weofodbote be hades<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.3"/> mæðe ⁊ hlaforde oððe cyningce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.4"/> be fullan mundbryce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.5-3"/>; oððe geladige hine mid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.6"/> fulre lade.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="340" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðæt man gehadodne man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.5-2"/> bende ne beate. Gyf hwa gehadodne man bende oððan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.1"/> beate oððon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.1"/> swyðe bismærige, bete wið hine, swa hit riht sy, ⁊ ðam bisceope weofodbote be ðæs hades mæðe ⁊ ðam laforde oððe þam kynincge be fullan mundbryce; oððe geladige [hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.2"/> sylfne] mid fulre lade.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="340" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa hadne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.2-4"/> man binde oððe beate oððe swiðe gebysmrige, bete wið hine, swa swa hit riht sy, ⁊ biscope wefodbote be hades mæðe ⁊ hlaforde oððe cyninge be fullan mundbrice; oððe geladige hine mid fulle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.1-4"/> lade.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="42" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="341" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis ordinatum aliquem uerberibus aut uinculis uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.15"/> aliquatenus affligat, emendet ei, sicut rectum sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.1-2"/>, et episcopo emendationem altaris secundum dignitatem ordinis, regi uel domino plenam infractionem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.2-2"/> pacis; aut plena lada neget.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="341" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis aliquem ordinatum ligauerit aut ceciderit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.14"/> aut turpiter deriserit, emendet illi secundum quod iustum est — scilicet secundum modum ordinis —, et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.1-5"/> episcopo altaris<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.2-5"/> emendationem, quod dicitur þeofodbote<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.3-2"/>, et domino aut regi plenum despectum, omnia ista secundum modum ordinis; aut purget se plena purgatione.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_42.lnote.oe.4-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="42" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="341" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis ordinatum liget aut [uerber]et aut nimiis contumeliis afficiat, primum satisfaciat ei secundum quod rectum est, deinde episcopo emendam altaris soluat iuxta ordinis dignitatem dominoque aut regi per plenam montam; aut pleno purgamine se purget.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="42" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="196" ed="#robertson"/>Ðæt man gehadodne man [ne]<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IICn_42.robnote.fn.7"/> bende ne beate. Gyf hwa gehadodne man bende oððan<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_42.robnote.fn.5"/> beate oððon<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_42.robnote.fn.5"/> swyðe bismærige<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#IICn_42.robnote.fn.8"/>, bete wið hine swa<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#IICn_42.robnote.fn.9"/> hit riht sy, ⁊ ðam<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_42.robnote.fn.2"/> bisceope weofodbote be ðæs<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_42.robnote.fn.2"/> hades mæðe, ⁊ ðam<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_42.robnote.fn.2"/> laforde oððe þam<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_42.robnote.fn.2"/> kynincge be fullan mundbryce, oððe geladige hine sylfne<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#IICn_42.robnote.fn.10"/> mid fulre lade.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="278" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gyf hwa gehadodne man bende oððon beate oððon swyðe gebysmrige, bete wið hine, swa swa hit riht sy, and bisceope weofodbote be hades mæðe and hlaforde oððe cyningce be fullan mundbryce; oððe geladige hine mid fulre lade.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="341" ed="#liebermann"/>(Dass man einen geweihten Mann [weder] binde noch schlage. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Wenn einer einen geweihten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_42.lnote.de.2"/> Mann bindet oder schlägt oder arg beschimpft, büsse er ihm gegenüber, wie es richtig ist, und dem Bischofe Altarbusse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_42.lnote.de.3"/> nach dem Grade der Weihe [des Verletzten], und dem [Immunitäts]herrn beziehungsweise dem König durch volle Busse für Bruch der Schutzherrlichkeit; oder er reinige sich durch vollen Reinigungsbeweis.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(That no one bind or beat a man in orders. B) If anyone binds or beats or grossly insults a man in orders, let him make amends to him as is right, and to the bishop with altar-compensation according to the rank of [the injured man's] orders, and to the [immunity-]lord or the king with full compensation for breach of protection; or let him clear himself with a full clearing.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_42.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="197" ed="#robertson"/>A man in holy orders shall not be bound or beaten. If anyone binds or beats or deeply insults a man in holy orders, he shall make amends towards him in accordance with the law, and shall pay the fine due to the bishop for sacrilege<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_42.robnote.n.2"/>, in accordance with the rank [of the injured man], and to his lord or to the king the full fine for breach of his <hi rend="italic">mund</hi>, or he shall clear himself by the full process of exculpation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_42.whinote.n.5"/><pb n="468" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone binds or beats or greatly insults a man in holy orders, he is to pay compensation to him as is right, and to the bishop the compensation for [insult to] the altar in proportion to its status, and to the lord or the king the full [fine for] breach of his protection; or he is to clear himself by full process of exculpation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="279" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If anyone binds or beats or greatly shames someone in holy orders, he shall make amends to him according to the law, and pay to the bishop the fine for assaulting an ecclesiastic according to the victim’s status, and to his lord or the king the full penalty for the violation of his protection; or he shall exonerate himself by the full oath of exculpation.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="341, 342"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_33">VIII Atr 33</ref>; <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_33">VIII Atr 33f.</ref></note>
